          <div class="delta"><strong>&lt;150 ms</strong> added average page-load overhead for already verified sessions.</div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="panel pipeline">
        <div class="pipeline-intro">
          <div>
            <div class="panel-kicker">Technical Core</div>
            <h2>Challenge-Based Verification Pipeline</h2>
            <p>Requests are assessed at the CDN edge before origin access. Low-risk humans proceed quickly; suspicious clients receive executable or interactive proof-of-work that many scripts cannot complete.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="latency-badge"><div class="big">&lt;2 sec</div><div class="small">typical end-to-end verification for legitimate human users</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="flow">
          <div class="stage"><div class="stage-num">1</div><h3>Request Interception</h3><p>Incoming HTTP traffic is routed through a nearby CDN edge node before content delivery.</p><div class="duration"><span>duration</span>&lt;50 ms</div></div>
          <div class="stage"><div class="stage-num">2</div><h3>Threat Scoring</h3><p>IP reputation, TLS fingerprint, session history, and behavioral signals are evaluated.</p><div class="stage-risk"><div class="pin"></div></div><div class="duration"><span>duration</span>~100 ms</div></div>
          <div class="stage"><div class="stage-num">3</div><h3>Challenge Issuance</h3><p>Risk above threshold triggers JavaScript or CAPTCHA-based verification.</p><div class="duration"><span>duration</span>~500 ms</div></div>
          <div class="stage"><div class="stage-num">4</div><h3>Verification Check</h3><p>Client response is validated and a traceable Ray ID is assigned for auditing.</p><div class="duration"><span>duration</span>~200 ms</div></div>
          <div class="stage"><div class="stage-num">5</div><h3>Access Grant</h3><p>Verified users are forwarded to origin with a session token; scripts lacking JS are blocked.</p><div class="duration"><span>duration</span>&lt;50 ms</div></div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="panel tradeoffs">
        <div class="panel-kicker">Nuance</div>
        <h2>Usability vs. Security Trade-offs</h2>
        <p>High-precision mitigation depends on operational choices that respect legitimate research workflows.</p>
        <div class="trade-grid">
          <div class="trade"><h3>Accessibility</h3><p>Challenge pages must satisfy WCAG 2.1 and avoid excluding users with disabilities.</p></div>
          <div class="trade"><h3>Institutional Access</h3><p>University IP ranges can be allowlisted to reduce unnecessary challenges for campus users.</p></div>
          <div class="trade"><h3>Transparency</h3><p>Clear verification messages explain brief delays without suggesting platform failure.</p></div>
          <div class="trade"><h3>Privacy</h3><p>Detection signals should be minimized and disclosed through clear data practices.</p></div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="panel takeaways">
        <div class="panel-kicker">Takeaways</div>
        <h2>What the evidence suggests</h2>
        <ul class="take-list">
          <li><span class="check">1</span><span>Bot traffic is now a first-order operational risk for academic publishers.</span></li>
          <li><span class="check">2</span><span>Multi-stage edge verification blocks most malicious automation with minimal human impact.</span></li>
          <li><span class="check">3</span><span>Traceable identifiers and metrics enable continuous security-usability optimization.</span></li>
          <li><span class="check">4</span><span>Publisher–CDN collaboration sustains open, secure access to scientific knowledge.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </section>

    <footer>
      <div class="source">Data summarized from the provided case brief: CDN-level bot mitigation for scientific publishing platforms such as www.science.org. Metrics compare pre/post deployment behavior under scraping and bot-surge conditions.</div>
      <div class="ray">Example trace: Ray ID 9edb9b44499904f9</div>
    </footer>
  </div>
